.TH VALLUM.TOML 5 "2026-10-19" "vallum 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
vallum.toml \- Vallum configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
[interface]
name = "vallum0"
private_key = "private.key"
addresses = ["10.7.0.1/24", "fd00:7::1/64"]
listen = "0.0.0.0:51820"
public_endpoint = "vpn.example.com:51820"
control = "/run/vallum/vallum0.sock"
fwmark = 4660

identity_issuer = "..."

[quick]
dns = ["1.1.1.1"]
dns_domain = "~."

[[peer]]
name = "laptop"
public_key = "vallum1:0003:..."
previous_public_key = "vallum1:0003:..."
endpoint = "vpn.example.com:51820"
allowed_ips = ["10.7.0.2/32"]
persistent_keepalive = 25
pin_endpoint = false
preshared_key_file = "laptop.psk"
.fi
.SH INTERFACE
.TP
.B addresses
One or both families; every address is assigned over netlink.
.TP
.B control
A 0600 Unix socket for the UAPI. Absent means no control plane. Use a unique
path per config; a relative path is resolved against the config directory, so
two configs in one directory with the same relative name collide.
.TP
.B fwmark
An \fBSO_MARK\fR for policy routing; applied before the privilege drop.
.TP
.B outer_mtu
The outer path MTU, default 1500; values above 1500 are refused.
.TP
.B user ", " group
Drop to these ids after the interface and socket exist.
.TP
.B identity_issuer
The CA's \fBvallum1:\fR public line (or the bare hex of its signing key).
When set, every peer's identity document must verify against it. When absent, a
document must be self-signed: a key binding with a window, not an authorisation.
.TP
.B public_endpoint
The address clients should dial, as `host:port`. The daemon does not read it —
a responder's reachable address is a property of its peers' configs. `server
init` writes the `--endpoint` it was given so every `peer add` bundle dials the
same address instead of re-detecting a source route.
.SH PEER
.TP
.B public_key " / " identity " / " identity_file
The peer's identity. Exactly one form: a \fBvallum1:\fR public line, an inline
document, or a file holding one. A document carries the key, a label and a
validity window.
.TP
.B previous_public_key " / " previous_identity " / " previous_identity_file
The identity a rotation still accepts. Written by `vallum peer rotate`, removed
by `vallum peer finalize`.
.TP
.B pin_endpoint
Refuse a handshake from any address other than \fBendpoint\fR. Requires an
endpoint. Closes the roaming-mischief case at the cost of NAT rebinding.
.TP
.B endpoint
An address or hostname; resolved at load, not periodically.
.TP
.B allowed_ips
Both the destinations routed to the peer and the sources accepted from it.
.TP
.B preshared_key " / " preshared_key_file
A 32-byte PSK, inline as 64 hex or in a 0600 file. Both is an error.
.SH QUICK
.TP
.B dns
Resolvers installed on the interface: through \fBresolvectl\fR when
systemd-resolved is running, otherwise through \fBresolvconf\fR.
.TP
.B dns_domain
The routing domain claimed when the interface owns the resolvers. Defaults to
\fB~.\fR on a full tunnel, which is what stops a query from leaking to the
local resolver.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vallum (8),
.BR vallum-quick (8)
